Xeno (non-affini) drugs (medicine or other substance that has a physiological effect when introduced into the body)

The Affini have developed thousands of drugs for ingestion, injection, and general consumption by xenosophonts as part of their wider efforts to ensure the happiness and wellbeing of everyone within the Compact.

There are _some_ pharmaceuticals developed by affini that are of particular note due to their effects. These drugs have been grouped into classes.

### **Xenodrug Classes**


In addition to the classes listed above, there are many medicines and drugs that fall outside of the defined classification system. One way of thinking about it as a writer could be to say that xenodrugs are “the kinky drugs”. Xenodrugs also strictly focused on non-affini sophonts: They’re drugs for pet species. 

Some of the common non-xenodrugs that show up in stories include the following:
- Existing drugs from a society that has been domesticated. Cannabis and booze are great for intox kink. Humans in HDG can and do consume them. But because they weren’t developed by Affini, they’re just drugs. Benzodiazepines help with anxiety, but they aren’t class-E drugs.
- Durotaxin and ATD (**add what ATD means here I can’t remember if it’s Affini Targeted Drugs or not**) Durotaxin is similar to liquor but for affini. ATD’s mimic xenodrug classes but for affini. Because they’re for affini and not xenosophonts, they’re not considered *xeno*drugs.
- Unclassified, strictly medicinal drugs. An Affini blood pressure medication isn’t a xenodrug, it’s just a medication because it doesn’t meet the kinky threshold. ***please fact check me on this point***

